Title: 0001-cmake-pthread-flag-optional
Repository: libwebp
Base-Version: 1.6.0 (libwebp-1.6.0.tar.gz, sha256 e4ab7009bf0629fd11982d4c2aa83964cf244cffba7347ecd39019a9e38c4564)
Requires: none
Author: aros-skia
Date: 2026-09-24
Upstream-Status: candidate (generic: probes the flag instead of assuming it)
Scope: AROS x86_64 ABIv11 static build (GCC 10.5.0). Build system only; no library code changes.

Problem:
  cmake/deps.cmake appends -pthread to CMAKE_C_FLAGS whenever FindThreads
  reports pthreads. x86_64-aros-gcc rejects the option ("unrecognized
  command-line option '-pthread'"), so every later configure check fails
  (unistd.h and the SSE2/SSE4.1 flag probes report "not found") and every
  object fails to compile.
Solution:
  Add -pthread only when check_c_compiler_flag accepts it. Linking pthreads
  is still carried by Threads::Threads (-lpthread on AROS, seeded in
  scripts/deps/aros-x86_64.cmake).
Validation:
  2026-09-24, scripts/deps/build.sh libwebp: configure finds unistd.h and
  SSE2/SSE4.1; libwebp.a, libwebpdecoder.a, libwebpdemux.a, libwebpmux.a,
  libsharpyuv.a install; the check program links with collect-aros
  (scripts/deps/check.sh libwebp).
Removal:
  When upstream probes the flag itself, or when the AROS compiler accepts
  -pthread.

--- a/cmake/deps.cmake
+++ b/cmake/deps.cmake
@@ -41,7 +41,13 @@
   if(Threads_FOUND)
     # work around cmake bug on QNX (https://cmake.org/Bug/view.php?id=11333)
     if(CMAKE_USE_PTHREADS_INIT AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "QNX")
-      set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} -pthread")
+      # Not every pthreads compiler knows -pthread (AROS GCC rejects it and
+      # links pthreads from libpthread.a via Threads::Threads instead).
+      include(CheckCCompilerFlag)
+      check_c_compiler_flag(-pthread WEBP_HAVE_FLAG_PTHREAD)
+      if(WEBP_HAVE_FLAG_PTHREAD)
+        set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} -pthread")
+      endif()
     endif()
     list(APPEND WEBP_DEP_LIBRARIES Threads::Threads)
   endif()
